MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_001: Dietrich. My soldiers tell me you delivered them from\ncertain death in the last battle.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_002: So they may say. I cut down the foes in front of me.\nThat is all I recall.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_003: I do not doubt it. The soldiers quaked to recall the\nviciousness with which you fought.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_004: Are those who serve you cowards? I had heard that\nwarriors of Saramis were brave.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_005: Most of them are. For these few, I imagine the\nincident was sobering.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_006: I thank you for sparing their lives. Name your reward\nand you shall have it.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_007: All I ask is a duel to the death. I have long craved to\nface you in a fair fight.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_008: You are a bold man to ask the life of a queen. But I\nam eager to test your strength.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_009: Very well then. I shall fight you. Prepare yourself.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_024: 
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_010: It is as I expected. Your spear is superb.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_011: As is your sword. Your style is unique, yet has clearly\nbeen refined to perfection.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_012: I have cut down all comers since I was a lad of nine.\nIt honed my sword. It goes where it will.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_013: And now its travels have taken it overseas? You have\ncome far, for a killer.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_014: I hear you were of noble stock in Fódlan. Was it wise\nto abandon your house in favor of the blade?
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_015: The house is not my concern. I have entrusted it to\nmy sister. She has the skill for it I lack.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_016: So you have a sister.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_017: I, too, went to battle in my youth. I hoped to prove\nmyself more in the field than in the palace.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_018: I brandished this spear for my people, for my\ncountry, and for Yu Phas. I take pride in these things.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_019: So the weight of your attacks comes from the weight\nof your obligations. Let us duel again so I may see.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_020: The burdens I bear... It was with these hands that I...
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_021: Why do you hesitate? The pleasures of battle call\nto us.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_022: Forgive me. I have lost the appetite for them. Let us\nleave our duel here for today.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_B_023: Hm...
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_001: Theodora. You have come. Let us duel.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_002: Wait. First, I would speak with you. You said last\ntime that my spear is driven by my many burdens.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_003: So I did. It is because of them that it has weight\nand strength.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_004: But some of my burdens overwhelmed me. Such as\nmy brother.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_005: Dyan tried to usurp the throne and threw Saramis\ninto disarray. And so...I beheaded him.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_006: Yet you lament that act.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_007: The decision was backed by all my subjects who put\ntheir faith in me. I have never thought it a mistake.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_008: But as a sister, to make the choice to kill one's own\nbrother...it is a hard thing.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_009: Do you think it is right, as queen, to give voice to\nthese misgivings? Your soldiers will lose faith.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_010: Normally I do not speak of it. But I judge that your\ndisinterest is so total that you will not repeat it.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_011: Heh.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_012: Saramis is a seafaring nation. Our ships go in and out\nof Fódlan and have brought news of House Lamine.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_013: About a killer brother and the sister who adores\nhim—a notorious pair even in that land. I envy you.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_014: You call us notorious. What of our notoriety\nis enviable?
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_015: Though you are feared by countless people, your\nbond as siblings remains firm.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_016: It was the opposite for me and my brother. But I\nwaste my breath speaking of this.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_017: From where I stand, you two are the same as us.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_018: How so? You should know that my brother and I\nwere on the worst possible terms.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_019: The first time I cut someone down, my sister was\nthere. She wept.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_020: It was me she wept for. She feared I would be\nconsumed by my deed—that I would be lost.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_021: Hm. She feared losing her connection to her brother\nmore than the slaughter before her?
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_022: She clung to me, caring not that I was spattered with\nblood. I told her not to cry.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_023: And she replied that she would not let go. Not until\nI swore I would not lose myself.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_024: She was always dear to me, of course. But since that\nday... My thoughts often turn to Elfrida.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_025: It is oddly steadfast of you to still keep a promise\nyou made at the age of nine.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_026: Dyan is in your thoughts too, is he not? Your spear\ncarries that weight.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_027: Were it not so, our duel would have ended with your\nhead upon the earth.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_028: When I first saw you, I thought you were merely a\npretty face. But there is substance beneath it.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_029: Were you not a vicious foreign killer, I might have\nhad you as a husband. If you could best me in a duel.
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_030: I'd not want to marry a headless bride, but if that is\nthe custom in Saramis...
MID_SE_Dit_Seo_A_031: Hah! I will hear no gibes from a man who has yet to\ncut off any of my limbs. Now draw your blade!